1:["$","$Le",null,{"guide":{"slug":"before-fish-home","number":"04","category":"FISH READINESS","title":"Before you bring fish home","intro":"Clear water alone does not tell you whether an aquarium is ready for fish. Check the filter, the test results and the needs of the fish you plan to keep.","image":"/mas-aquarium-studio/aquarium.jpg","alt":"A planted freshwater aquarium with filtration and aquatic plants","takeaway":"Bring your water-test history and fish shortlist to the shop before purchase.","sections":[{"id":"filter","title":"Understand what the filter needs to do","body":"Biological filtration relies on established bacteria to process ammonia into nitrite and then nitrate. Ammonia and nitrite are harmful to fish. A new filter needs to establish this capacity."},{"id":"readiness","title":"Use test results to assess readiness","body":"Check that cycling is established and ammonia and nitrite read zero, with the other water conditions suitable for your chosen species. Ask the shop to interpret your test history. One zero reading from a freshly filled tank does not demonstrate filter capacity."},{"id":"compatibility","title":"Review the fish as a group","body":"Discuss adult size, temperament, social needs and compatibility. Introduce fish at a pace your established filtration can support, while meeting the needs of the selected species."},{"id":"journey","title":"Plan the journey home","body":"Before purchase, ask about transport, acclimatisation and the care your chosen fish will need. Keep the shop’s guidance with your setup record so you can refer to it at home."}],"questions":["Do my test records show that the aquarium is ready?","Will these fish suit each other and my tank?","How should I transport and introduce these fish?"],"sources":[{"title":"RSPCA Australia — Aquarium water quality","url":"https://kb.rspca.org.au/categories/companion-animals/fish/why-is-water-quality-important-when-setting-up-a-fish-aquarium"},{"title":"RSPCA Australia — Tropical fish care","url":"https://kb.rspca.org.au/categories/companion-animals/fish/how-should-i-care-for-my-tropical-fish"}],"next":"first-aquarium-checklist","shopPlants":false}}]
